OpenCMR2 for WarpOS (PowerPC)
=============================

A WarpOS port of OpenCMR2, a reimplementation of the engine of Colin McRae
Rally 2.0, for Amigas with a PowerPC accelerator and a Radeon 9200. It needs
the original PC game data; none is included.

Contents
--------

  opencmr2                    the game (WarpOS executable)
  OpenCMR2-WOS                the launch script; start the game with it
  LICENSE                     OpenCMR2 licence (GNU GPL version 3)

Requirements
------------

  - AmigaOS 3.x with WarpOS (powerpc.library) and a PowerPC accelerator,
    603e or better. Tested only on an A4000 with a 68060 and an MPC7410;
    expect a slower frame rate on 603e and 604e boards.
  - A Radeon 9200 with Radeon9200.chip and Prometheus.card.
  - The PPC MiniGL R200 stack from its MiniGLWOS-aligned version on
    (dispatch ABI 5, 840-byte table): minigl_ppc.dll and minigl_ppc_host
    in the game drawer, minigl.library in LIBS:. Not included.
    The game is built on the same MiniGL headers as MiniGLWOS (Aminet
    util/libs/MiniGLWOS_Classic, for Warp3D cards), so it should also run
    with that minigl_ppc.dll; this is untested.
  - AHI 4 (no AHI means no sound).
  - The original PC installation of Colin McRae Rally 2.0.

Installing
----------

1. Make a COPY of the PC installation on an Amiga drive. Do not use your
   only copy: the Amiga version writes its settings and driver profiles in
   its own format, which the PC version cannot read (and the other way
   round). Saved games are kept apart from PC saves.
2. Copy opencmr2 and OpenCMR2-WOS into that copy, next to the game data,
   and put minigl_ppc.dll and minigl_ppc_host there too.
3. Start the game from a Shell in that drawer:

     Execute OpenCMR2-WOS

   The script sets the MiniGL stack's options (ENV:MGLPPC_*) and the stack
   size; starting opencmr2 directly skips them. minigl_ppc.dll starts
   minigl_ppc_host by itself.

Settings are in opencmr2.ini in the game drawer, created on the first start.
The game's own Options, Graphics, Advanced graphics options, draw distance
trades detail for frame rate (one step lower gives about 66 fps at the start
of the first Rally Finland stage on the test machine, against 50).

Quitting
--------

Quit from the game menu. Do not Break a WarpOS program from the Shell; if
the game does not answer, SetEnv OPENCMR2_QUIT 1 in another Shell asks it
to quit. After a failed run, power the machine off and on before trusting
the next result: the graphics card keeps its state across a warm reset.
